  "body": "## Independent enclosure of the pivot-566+554 T74 complex root (no new \u03ba)\n\n**Card:** `independent-moment` (independent-verification track, scope key `c6f2494b197df3bc3591`, chooser OS nonce `9dd43e38694b6907874fe4e993da7bf9`, priority revision 3). Scope **changed**, with the reason in `TASK.json`. Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18927871. Base `ae95f60feec79897b153dba6459bb3f9fd4d7b8e`. Adds only `research/t74-k554-root-enclosure/`.\n\n### Why this object\n\nThe selected https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1094 pricing already has independent ledger, moment, invoice and outer checks (frontier1094-emitted-ledger-seed78, selected-suppliers-de-diagnostic, pr1407-complex-moment-audit-seed39, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1735). So I applied the card's enclosure method to the pending supplier behind the highest open claims.\n\nEvery claim from https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1800 to https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928 prices the pivot-566+554 T74 supplier. At their \"free \u03b5 \u2192 1\" point, \u03ba approaches this supplier's complex moment root. https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928 sets b to its certified native endpoint minus 10^-10010. Until now, only the authors' own engines had certified that endpoint.\n\n### What is checked\n\nThe inputs are the global profile `{1:1560432, 2:336336, 3:278724, 4:84912, 5:54612, 8:5328, 48:22748}`, m = 73 and W = 66304. They are pinned by Git blob and SHA-256 from `new/SPEC.json` at https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1672 (head `b8ab040d`) and https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928 (head `07e4e423`). `extract_inputs.py --check` rebuilds `INPUTS.json` byte for byte from the fetched pull refs.\n\nThe moment definitions come from the written review rather than code: native moment from `research/native-complex-moment552/PROOF.md`, conservative fallback from `notes/three-stage-cover-assembly.tex`.\n\nThe method shares no algorithm with the authors' Mercator and binary-reduction engines or with earlier audits:\n\n- ln 2, ln 3 and ln 5 are integer combinations of ln(16/15), ln(25/24) and ln(81/80). Each of these is 2 atanh(1/k), and the verifier checks the identities exactly.\n- ln 73 = ln 72 + 2 atanh(1/145).\n- exp uses argument halving, a Taylor polynomial with a tail bound, and repeated squaring.\n- All values are outward-rounded integers. The final comparison is exact. Undecided signs fail closed.\n\n| Case | Grid | Bits | M(e) | M(e + grid) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [1672](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1672) native | 1e-70 | 360 | below 1 | above 1 |\n| [1672](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1672) conservative | 1e-70 | 360 | below 1 | above 1 |\n| [1928](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928) native | 1e-10000 | 33347 | below 1 | above 1 |\n| [1928](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928) conservative | 1e-10000 | 33347 | below 1 | above 1 |\n\nAlso checked:\n\n- For both models, the 1e-70 endpoints equal the 1e-70 floors of the 1e-10000 endpoints.\n- At both heads, 249 gauge44 calls and 417 extra calls with their per-call profiles, plus 22,748 idle rank-48 children, sum to the global profile. Rank mass is 4,816,512 and the deficit is 23,680.\n- The headline \u03ba of CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1928 is 2.003e-10010 below its native endpoint, as its choice of b implies. CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1672's is 2.817e-6 below.\n- Ten semantic controls are rejected: next and previous grid point as endpoint, one child moved from rank 1 to rank 2, m = 72, W \u2212 1, and the surcharge omitted or added in the wrong model. Three are repeated at 1e-10000.\n\nThe optional `crosscheck_decimal.py` repeats the 1e-10000 case with Python's `decimal` ln and exp at 10,060 digits. It agrees on all seven log enclosures and all four signs. It takes about 4 minutes and corroborates the result; it is not a certificate.\n\n**No discrepancy was found.**\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-k554-root-enclosure --check-only\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-k554-root-enclosure\n```\n\nLocal results on Windows, Python 3.12, stdlib only:\n\n```\nPASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS (not a mathematical acceptance check)\nPASS_T74_K554_ROOT_ENCLOSURE_INDEPENDENT | brackets 4 | nesting 2 | controls 10 rejected | 13.5 s\nRan 10 tests ... OK\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/t74-k554-root-enclosure outcome=completed\nPASS_DECIMAL_CROSSCHECK | 7 log enclosures | 4 moment signs agree\nPASS_INPUTS_MATCH_PINNED_PR_HEADS\n```\n\n`tests.test_research_onboarding`, `tests.test_research_replay_selection` and `tests.test_research_assignment` also pass (32 tests). `make` is not installed on this host, so no make target was run. Hosted CI has not run.\n\n### Scope\n\nThis is a finite check of recorded endpoints and of the profile arithmetic. The following are taken as given:\n\n- the profiles themselves;\n- the native, surcharge-free complex recurrence;\n- the outer reduction from b to \u03ba, the fine source-prime padding and the \u03b5 \u2192 1 transfer (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1797 audits the CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1786 lemmas on a different supplier);\n- all inherited all-size/compiler, realization, hosting, precision/tape, recovery, analytic and bit H1-H5 assumptions.\n\nNo new \u03ba is claimed and the selected record is unchanged.\n\n### Open next questions\n\n1. Does CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1928's `outer/LEDGER.json` follow from this endpoint, checked by code that does not import `outer/*.py`?\n2. Does the global profile equal the profile emitted by the T74 template and owner map? The seed78 emitted-ledger rebuild could be adapted to the two-provider layout.\n\n### Credit\n\n- Supplier: mdumitrean (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1625), Jeremy Kothe (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1672 through https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1928), Rohan Arun (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1319) and their credited lineage.\n- Outer: Vlado Vojdanovski (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1673) and chafreaky (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1786).\n- Audit pattern: Sagar Thakrar's seed78 package and the earlier independent moment packages.\n\nPrepared by **Aaron Wang**, with help from opencode. Apache-2.0.\n\nWorkflow feedback: the overlap search finds claims by \u03ba digits but not \"who has independently checked this number\". A per-claim \"independent checks\" field in the PR ledger would have saved most of the 30-minute survey.\n",
